{
  "version": 1,
  "constants": {"PCM_STALE_AFTER":45000},
  "note": "D52.4/D52.5 app-side audio transport watchdog (SPEC.md \"Audio transport liveness\"). Monotonic milliseconds. frames lists what arrives in order: track/audio/sources/trackEnd/stop on the recording's audio transport (id names the span), control is any frame on the control connection (ping/pong, meetings, status, result, hello). All spans are remote browser spans. Every audio-transport frame counts; control frames do not. The watchdog is armed only while an open span (track, not yet trackEnd or stop) has delivered audio. closeAtMs is when the app closes the transport (now - lastFrame >= PCM_STALE_AFTER while armed), or null if it never does (a frame arriving exactly at the deadline is too late); probes give closed-by-then at exact times, including the 1 ms before the boundary. The app closes through its EOF path (system/lost fallback).",
  "cases": [
